# Build output. Anchored with a leading slash: a bare "aboard" pattern also
# matches any DIRECTORY named aboard, which silently excluded both
# .claude/skills/aboard/ — the whole skill — and pkg/aboard/ from the repo.
/aboard
/dist/

# Everything the board owns for this project: the state document, the images the
# human pasted, and the machine-local runtime files (instance record, journal,
# sidecar logs, screenshots). One path, because there is one directory.
#
# A board is a LOCAL, PERSISTENT, NON-AUTHORITATIVE channel. Committing it would
# mean a whole-file JSON conflict on every merge, over a conversation that was
# never the other developer's.
/.aboard/

# Local cross-module development (go.work). Never a committed replace directive.
/go.work
/go.work.sum
